            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for to be at a loss, then the Gujarati for to disperse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: સમાચાર",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સમાચાર — samācār — \"the news\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મેં સવારે સમાચાર સાંભળ્યા. mẽ savāre samācār sā̃bhaḷyā. I listened to the news this morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun, used in the plural."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સમાચાર (samācār) is a tatsama, Sanskrit samācāra, \"procedure, conduct, custom\" (Monier-Williams); the sense \"news\" is the modern language's. The verb with it is plural: સમાચાર સાંભળ્યા."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
